  <p class="gd-byline" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--blue-soft);opacity:.9;margin:16px 0 0">By <a href="/about" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Heliski Travel Team</a> · Updated 5 Aug 2026</p>
  <p class="gd-lede">Iceland's backcountry is quietly one of the best on earth: Arctic ridgelines that fall all the way to the sea, deep spring snow, and daylight that stretches towards midnight. You can experience it three ways, ski touring under your own power, heli-assisted touring, or full heli-skiing, and this guide explains each one, the terrain of the Troll Peninsula, the season and how to do it safely with Heliski Travel. When you are ready, see the <a href="/heli-assisted-touring">heli-assisted touring trips</a>.</p>
